<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Abdul Samad of Selangor</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1804">1804</a>–<a href="/years/1898">1898</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Sultan Abdul Samad</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Abdul Samad of Selangor was the fourth <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> of Selangor, reigning from 1857 to 1898. His reign saw the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tin">tin</a> rush that drew Chinese miners into the Klang valley and the civil war among Selangor chiefs known as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/klang-war">Klang War</a>. In 1874 he accepted a British Resident, bringing Selangor under British <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indirect-rule">indirect rule</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/abdul-samad-of-selangor.jpg" alt="Abdul Samad of Selangor" width="320" height="419" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Lambert &amp;amp; Co., G.R. / Singapore · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:KITLV_-_7248_-_Lambert_%26_Co.,_G.R._-_Singapore_-_Sir_Abdul_Samad,_Sultan_of_Selangor_-_circa_1890.tif" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
